---
import SiteLayout from '../../../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';

const groups = [
  {
    heading: 'Old Town anchors',
    intro: 'The walkable heart of it — where most visitors end up eating.',
    places: [
      { name: 'The Mockingbird Cafe', meta: 'Coffee · cafe · Second St', note: 'A coffee shop, cafe, and art space in an old building two blocks off the beach, open since the year after Katrina. Sandwiches, salads, good coffee, and a courtyard that&rsquo;s a perfect slow-morning spot. The local gathering place — start your day here.' },
      { name: 'The Sycamore House', meta: 'New American · Main St · dinner only', note: 'The grown-up dinner in town, family-run since 2002 in an old boarding house with a screen porch. Gulf seafood and New Orleans–leaning plates, open just a few evenings a week. Call ahead and reserve — it&rsquo;s small and the hours are limited.' },
      { name: '200 North Beach', meta: 'Seafood · steaks · harbor-front', note: 'Fresh seafood, pasta, and steaks in a restored 1903 building across from the municipal harbor, with some of the best water views in Old Town. The nice sit-down option that isn&rsquo;t fussy about it.' },
    ],
  },
  {
    heading: 'On the water',
    intro: 'Beach-bar energy, harbor views, and live music on the weekends.',
    places: [
      { name: 'The Blind Tiger', meta: 'Beach bar & grill · harbor-front', note: 'Open-air spot on the marina front with big views of the harbor, in-house brews, and live music on the patio most weekends. Get the royal reds or the barbecued oysters. Family-friendly and very Bay St. Louis.' },
      { name: 'Buoy&rsquo;s Bar', meta: 'Burgers · beach-front', note: 'A nautical-themed watering hole right on the beach. People rave about the burger and garlic fries, and on some weekends there&rsquo;s live music you can catch with your feet practically in the sand.' },
    ],
  },
  {
    heading: 'Gulf seafood (obviously)',
    intro: 'You&rsquo;re on the Coast. This part is mandatory.',
    places: [
      { name: 'Cuz&rsquo;s Old Town Oyster Bar & Grill', meta: 'Oysters · seafood · Beach Blvd', note: 'Family-owned and casual, with the bayou-flavor lineup people drive in for — boiled shrimp, fried oysters, crawfish étouffée, crab claws, and gumbo. The no-frills seafood meal you came to the Coast for.' },
    ],
  },
];
---

<SiteLayout
  title="Best Restaurants in Bay St. Louis, MS — Where to Eat in Old Town | Rob Recio"
  description="A Coast writer&rsquo;s guide to eating in Bay St. Louis, Mississippi — The Mockingbird Cafe, Sycamore House, the harbor-front spots, and the Gulf seafood worth the drive west."
  robots="noindex, nofollow, noarchive, nosnippet"
>

  <main class="guide">

    <header class="guide-hero">
      <p class="eyebrow"><a href="/explore" class="crumb">Explore</a> · <a href="/explore/bay-st-louis" class="crumb">Bay St. Louis</a> · Food &amp; Dining</p>
      <h1>Where to eat in Bay St. Louis, <em>from someone who covers this Coast.</em></h1>
      <p class="lede">Bay St. Louis eats like a town that knows it&rsquo;s a destination but hasn&rsquo;t gotten precious about it. Old Town is small enough to walk between most of the good spots, the seafood is right off the Gulf, and nobody&rsquo;s judging your flip-flops. Here&rsquo;s where I&rsquo;d send you — show up hungry.</p>
    </header>

    {groups.map(g => (
      <section class="guide-section">
        <h2>{g.heading}</h2>
        <p class="section-sub">{g.intro}</p>
        <div class="place-list">
          {g.places.map(p => (
            <div class="place">
              <div class="place-head">
                <h3>{p.name}</h3>
                <span class="place-meta">{p.meta}</span>
              </div>
              <p>{p.note}</p>
            </div>
          ))}
        </div>
      </section>
    ))}

    <section class="guide-section">
      <h2>The deal</h2>
      <p>Bay St. Louis isn&rsquo;t trying to be New Orleans, even though it&rsquo;s only an hour away. It&rsquo;s its own thing — an artsy little beach town where the dinner spots are casual and the harbor is the view. Reservations really only matter at Sycamore House, and only because it&rsquo;s small and open a few nights a week. When you&rsquo;re done eating, the <a href="/explore/bay-st-louis/activities">things-to-do guide</a> and the <a href="/explore/bay-st-louis/exploration">outdoors guide</a> pick up from here.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="cta-block">
      <h2>Eating your way down the Coast?</h2>
      <p>I track new openings, pop-ups, and the spots worth the drive across all three counties in <strong>The Seawall</strong>, my twice-weekly Coast newsletter.</p>
      <div class="cta-buttons">
        <a href="/explore/bay-st-louis" class="btn btn-primary">More Bay St. Louis guides</a>
        <a href="mailto:robrecio@gmail.com" class="btn btn-ghost">Ask Rob</a>
      </div>
      <p class="cta-note">Rob Recio lives in Ocean Springs and is in real-estate-licensure training in Mississippi. This is informational visitor content, not real-estate advice or a solicitation.</p>
    </section>

    <aside class="sources">
      <h3>Good to know</h3>
      <p class="sources-note"><strong>Verified May 2026.</strong> Restaurants come and go and hours shift with the season — call ahead for anything time-sensitive, especially Sycamore House&rsquo;s limited dinner nights. Spotted a place that closed or one I&rsquo;m missing? <a href="mailto:robrecio@gmail.com">Let me know</a> and I&rsquo;ll update it.</p>
    </aside>

  </main>

</SiteLayout>

<style>
  .guide { max-width: var(--max); margin: 0 auto; padding: 3rem 1.5rem 4rem; }
  .guide-hero { max-width: var(--max-prose); margin: 0 auto 3rem; text-align: left; }
  .eyebrow {
    font-size: 0.78rem; font-weight: 600; text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em; color: var(--gulf); margin-bottom: 1.2rem;
  }
  .crumb { color: var(--gulf); text-decoration: none; }
  .crumb:hover { text-decoration: underline; }
  .guide-hero h1 {
    font-family: var(--serif); font-weight: 600;
    font-size: clamp(2.25rem, 4.8vw, 3.4rem); line-height: 1.07;
    letter-spacing: -0.022em; color: var(--ink);
  }
  .guide-hero h1 em { font-style: italic; color: var(--gulf-deep); }
  .lede { font-size: 1.18rem; color: var(--ink-soft); margin-top: 1.5rem; line-height: 1.6; }

  .guide-section { max-width: var(--max-prose); margin: 0 auto; padding: 2.5rem 0; border-top: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .guide-section h2 {
    font-family: var(--serif); font-weight: 600;
    font-size: clamp(1.6rem, 3.2vw, 2.1rem); line-height: 1.15;
    letter-spacing: -0.018em; color: var(--ink); margin-bottom: 0.6rem;
  }
  .section-sub { color: var(--ink-soft); font-size: 1.05rem; margin-bottom: 1.6rem; line-height: 1.6; }
  .guide-section > p { font-size: 1.06rem; color: var(--ink-soft); line-height: 1.7; margin-bottom: 1.1rem; }

  .place-list { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.8rem; }
  .place {
    background: var(--paper); border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-left: 3px solid var(--gulf); border-radius: 0 10px 10px 0;
    padding: 1.1rem 1.3rem;
  }
  .place-head { display: flex; align-items: baseline; justify-content: space-between; gap: 0.8rem; flex-wrap: wrap; margin-bottom: 0.4rem; }
  .place h3 { font-family: var(--serif); font-weight: 600; font-size: 1.18rem; color: var(--ink); }
  .place-meta { font-size: 0.8rem; color: var(--gulf-deep); font-weight: 500; text-align: right; }
  .place p { font-size: 0.97rem; color: var(--ink-soft); line-height: 1.6; margin: 0; }

  .cta-block {
    max-width: var(--max-prose); margin: 4rem auto 0; padding: 2.5rem 2rem;
    background: var(--paper); border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 14px; text-align: center;
  }
  .cta-block h2 { font-family: var(--serif); font-weight: 600; font-size: 1.8rem; color: var(--ink); margin-bottom: 0.8rem; }
  .cta-block p { color: var(--ink-soft); font-size: 1.05rem; margin: 0 auto 1.5rem; max-width: 600px; }
  .cta-block p strong { color: var(--ink); }
  .cta-buttons { display: flex; gap: 0.8rem; justify-content: center; flex-wrap: wrap; margin-bottom: 1.5rem; }
  .cta-note { font-size: 0.82rem !important; color: var(--ink-soft) !important; font-style: italic; margin-bottom: 0 !important; }

  .sources {
    max-width: var(--max-prose); margin: 2.5rem auto 0; padding: 1.4rem 1.6rem;
    background: var(--sand); border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 12px;
  }
  .sources h3 {
    font-family: var(--serif); font-weight: 600; font-size: 1rem; color: var(--ink);
    text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.12em; margin-bottom: 0.6rem;
  }
  .sources-note { font-size: 0.88rem; color: var(--ink-soft); font-style: italic; margin: 0; line-height: 1.6; }
</style>
